# Written by PanelAlpha, and small on purpose.
#
# CouchCMS is served from the root of the checkout, so every file the deploy
# leaves beside the application is a URL. The generated vhost already denies
# the ones it knows about -- dotfiles (.git, .env, the admin password),
# `docker-compose.yml` and anything named `panelalpha-*` -- but its rule reads
#
#     ^(?:docker-compose\.ya?ml|panelalpha[-.])
#
# which does not match `docker-compose.override.yml`, the file the engine
# writes from a recipe's overrides/. Served as plain text it publishes the
# deploy's own arrangement, and a recipe that put a value in it would publish
# that too.
#
# Anchored on the name rather than on a wildcard, so a page called
# `compose-guide.yml` is still the site's to serve.
<FilesMatch "^docker-compose\.">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# CouchCMS generates its own .htaccess for Pretty URLs -- couch/gen_htaccess.php
# writes one and tells you to put it in the root of your site, which is this
# file. If you do that, keep the block above.
